    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world logic—something I can’t ignore but also find fascinating when broken down into patterns. My parents’ education levels made it tricky, but my curiosity for biology and philosophy keeps me engaged. It’s not just numbers; it’s problem-solving that connects to everything else.",
